{"timestamp": "2025-07-28T14:04:05.377116", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "", "island_id": 2, "scores": {"3": -1}}
{"timestamp": "2025-07-28T14:05:20.502284", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  current_state = env._current_state\n  cookbook_index = env.world.cookbook.index\n\n  # 1. Get Primitive Index\n  primitive_idx = cookbook_index[primitive]\n  if primitive_idx is None:\n      # This primitive doesn't exist in the cookbook or is an invalid name.\n      return []\n\n  # 2. Check if the primitive is actually grabbable.\n  # If it's in the non_grabbable_indices set, it cannot be collected via the 'USE' action\n  # in the sense of picking it up. The 'collect' function implies obtaining an item.\n  if primitive_idx in env.world.non_grabbable_indices:\n      return []\n\n  # 3. Get Action Mappings dynamically from the environment.\n  action_map = env.action_specs()\n  UP_ACTION = action_map['UP']\n  DOWN_ACTION = action_map['DOWN']\n  LEFT_ACTION = action_map['LEFT']\n  RIGHT_ACTION = action_map['RIGHT']\n  USE_ACTION = action_map['USE']\n\n  # 4. Check Inventory: If the primitive is already collected, no actions are needed.\n  if current_state.inventory[primitive_idx] > 0:\n      return []\n\n  # 5. Initialize BFS for pathfinding.\n  start_y, start_x = current_state.pos # Agent's current position (y, x)\n  grid = current_state.grid\n  HEIGHT, WIDTH, _ = grid.shape\n\n  # 6. Define impassable terrain types for pathfinding.\n  # This set includes all non-grabbable entities, *except* for workshops,\n  # as workshops are typically traversable locations.\n  # Explicitly add water and stone for robustness, as they are almost universally impassable.\n  impassable_kinds = set(env.world.non_grabbable_indices) - set(env.world.workshop_indices)\n  if env.world.water_index is not None:\n      impassable_kinds.add(env.world.water_index)\n  if env.world.stone_index is not None:\n      impassable_kinds.add(env.world.stone_index)\n\n  # Queue stores tuples: (current_y, current_x)\n  q = collections.deque([(start_y, start_x)])\n  # Dictionary to reconstruct path: (current_y, current_x) -> (parent_y, parent_x, action_taken_to_reach_current_node)\n  # This implicitly serves as the 'visited' set, as we only add to parent if not already visited.\n  parent = {(start_y, start_x): (None, None, None)}\n\n  # Define possible movements (dy, dx) and their corresponding action IDs.\n  # Assuming (y, x) corresponds to (row, column) in a 2D grid.\n  move_deltas = [\n      (-1, 0, UP_ACTION),    # Move Up (decrease y)\n      (1, 0, DOWN_ACTION),   # Move Down (increase y)\n      (0, -1, LEFT_ACTION),  # Move Left (decrease x)\n      (0, 1, RIGHT_ACTION)   # Move Right (increase x)\n  ]\n\n  while q:\n      curr_y, curr_x = q.popleft()\n\n      # Check if the current position is adjacent to the primitive.\n      # The 'USE' action typically operates on items in the 3x3 neighborhood\n      # around the agent's current position, as implied by CraftState.next_to.\n      is_adjacent_to_primitive = False\n      for dy_adj in [-1, 0, 1]:\n          for dx_adj in [-1, 0, 1]:\n              check_y, check_x = curr_y + dy_adj, curr_x + dx_adj\n              # Ensure the checked coordinates are within grid bounds.\n              if 0 <= check_y < HEIGHT and 0 <= check_x < WIDTH:\n                  # Check if the primitive exists at this neighboring location.\n                  # The grid stores 1 if the kind is present, 0 otherwise.\n                  if grid[check_y, check_x, primitive_idx] == 1:\n                      is_adjacent_to_primitive = True\n                      break\n          if is_adjacent_to_primitive:\n              break\n\n      if is_adjacent_to_primitive:\n          # This cell (curr_y, curr_x) is adjacent to the primitive.\n          # Found the shortest path to a position where 'USE' can be performed.\n          \n          # Reconstruct the path from start_pos to (curr_y, curr_x)\n          path_actions = []\n          current_node = (curr_y, curr_x)\n          while current_node != (start_y, start_x):\n              # For the start node, its parent is (None, None, None), so we stop there.\n              prev_y, prev_x, action_to_curr = parent[current_node]\n              path_actions.append(action_to_curr)\n              current_node = (prev_y, prev_x)\n          path_actions.reverse() # Path is built in reverse order, so reverse it.\n          \n          return path_actions + [USE_ACTION] # Append USE_ACTION at the end.\n\n      # Explore adjacent cells for movement if no target found yet.\n      for dy_move, dx_move, action_to_take in move_deltas:\n          next_y, next_x = curr_y + dy_move, curr_x + dx_move\n\n          # Check if the next cell is within bounds and has not been visited yet.\n          if 0 <= next_y < HEIGHT and 0 <= next_x < WIDTH and (next_y, next_x) not in parent:\n              # Check if the next cell is traversable.\n              # A cell is traversable if it does not contain any of the explicitly defined impassable kinds.\n              is_traversable = True\n              for i_kind in impassable_kinds:\n                  if grid[next_y, next_x, i_kind] == 1: # If this kind is present at the cell\n                      is_traversable = False\n                      break\n              \n              if is_traversable:\n                  parent[(next_y, next_x)] = (curr_y, curr_x, action_to_take)\n                  q.append((next_y, next_x))\n\n  # If the BFS completes and no path to an adjacent primitive was found,\n  # it means the primitive is either not on the map or unreachable.\n  return []", "island_id": 6, "scores": {"3": 0.0}}
